# Repository root: D:\Desktop\Food  -- the project's real root, not `AcouDiet/`.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS THE MOST IMPORTANT ONE IN THE REPO (ADR-36)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# This project had **no version control at all** until ADR-36, and its own ADR log records at least
# two irreversible losses caused by that -- e.g. "旧包已被 Copy-Item 覆盖，本仓不是 git 仓库，
# 取不回旧字节", and ADR-34's Qwen removal had to be hand-archived before anything could be deleted.
#
# The reason nobody had committed is visible below: the tree carries ~6 GB of build output and
# vendored toolchains, and the *authoritative* material is spread across three sibling directories
# (`shared/` = the SSOT, `docs/` = the frozen SPEC tree + the ADR log, `AcouDiet/` = the code).
# A repo rooted at `AcouDiet/` alone would not version the ADR log or `shared/feature_config.json`,
# i.e. it would not version the two things this project treats as its constitution.
#
# Ignoring the heavy directories below makes the real sources (a few MB) committable.

# ---- Toolchains (outside the deliverable on purpose) -------------------------------------
_toolchain/
AcouDiet/_toolchain/
*.gguf

# ---- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------------------
AcouDiet/app/build/
AcouDiet/app/.dart_tool/
AcouDiet/app/.flutter-plugins
AcouDiet/app/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
AcouDiet/app/.packages
AcouDiet/build/
AcouDiet/_build/
AcouDiet/ai/data/raw/
AcouDiet/ai/data/augmented/
AcouDiet/ai/data/parity_out/

# ---- Review artefacts --------------------------------------------------------------------
# `app/tool/visual_capture_test.dart` renders the real pages to PNG so the UI work can be reviewed
# against `软件UI界面设计图/*.png` without a device (ADR-38). The renders are derived output: one
# command regenerates them, and the *checks* that must stay green are the widget tests, not the
# pixels.
AcouDiet/app/tool/visual_capture/

# ---- Release artifacts -------------------------------------------------------------------
# APKs are 60-600 MB and reproducible from source + the model card; `dist/*.sha256` plus the
# release docs record what was shipped and what it hashed to. See ADR-36 for the honest limitation
# of this choice: a *rebuilt* APK still overwrites its predecessor, so the hash ledger in
# `docs/demo/PHONE_INSTALL.md` is what preserves "which bytes were ever released".
AcouDiet/dist/*.apk
AcouDiet/dist/*.apk.sha256

# ---- Android / Gradle / signing ----------------------------------------------------------
AcouDiet/app/android/.gradle/
AcouDiet/app/android/local.properties
AcouDiet/app/android/key.properties
AcouDiet/app/android/app/debug/
AcouDiet/app/android/app/profile/
AcouDiet/app/android/app/release/
*.jks
*.keystore

# ---- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ---- Large binaries that are inputs, not source ------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.docx
# Training/inference checkpoints: 511 MB and 31 MB here, and the on-device language model they
# belonged to was removed in ADR-34. `*.tflite` files are deliberately NOT ignored -- they are
# the shipped artifact (4 MB) and committing them is what makes a rebuild reproducible.
*.safetensors
tokenizer.json

# ---- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
